# Annotation Technologies: A Software and Research Review.

**Authors:** Wolfe, Joanna

## Abstract
Describes a range of currently available and developing technologies for creating and presenting annotations, glosses, and other comments on digital documents. Discusses the potential applications of these tools for providing feedback to student writers, supporting extended group discussions around digital texts, and facilitating research and reading-to-write tasks. Compares and evaluates different software programs. (SG)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ659082

